From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Winter21c <winter21c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Oct 2025 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pylibfdt: use the Python 3 C API instead of the Py2 aliases

SWIG 4.5.0 removed the Python 2 compatibility macros (PyInt_*, PyString_*)
that it used to emit into every wrapper. libfdt.i relies on those macros, so
pylibfdt no longer compiles:

    libfdt_wrap.c: error: implicit declaration of function 'PyInt_AsLong'
    libfdt_wrap.c: error: implicit declaration of function 'PyString_FromString'

pylibfdt is not optional for us: uboot-rockchip sets UBOOT_USE_INTREE_DTC=1
so that the in-tree dtc/pylibfdt is used, and the failure shows up as

    make[6]: *** [scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/Makefile:33:rebuild] Error 1
    make[4]: *** [Makefile:2318: scripts_dtc] Error 2

which reads like a board or toolchain problem but is neither.

Replace the three uses with their Python 3 equivalents. This is safe on
Python 3 by definition (SWIG's removed macros were aliases to exactly these
functions), and this code path is already Python-3-only -- the surrounding
%#if PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x03000000 blocks say so.

The same change is what dtc upstream and the Yocto/OE u-boot recipe carry,
so this patch can be dropped once u-boot updates its bundled copy.

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter21c@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/pylibfdt/libfdt.i_shipped
@@ -1033,7 +1033,7 @@
 	PyObject *buff;
 
 	if ($1) {
-		resultobj = PyString_FromString(
+		resultobj = PyUnicode_FromString(
 			fdt_string(fdt1, fdt32_to_cpu($1->nameoff)));
 		buff = PyByteArray_FromStringAndSize(
 			(const char *)($1 + 1), fdt32_to_cpu($1->len));
@@ -1064,13 +1064,13 @@
         }
         $1 = PyBytes_AsString($input);
     %#else
-        $1 = PyString_AsString($input);   /* char *str */
+        $1 = PyBytes_AsString($input);   /* char *str */
     %#endif
 }
 
 /* typemaps used for fdt_next_node() */
 %typemap(in, numinputs=1) int *depth (int depth) {
-   depth = (int) PyInt_AsLong($input);
+   depth = (int) PyLong_AsLong($input);
    $1 = &depth;
 }
 
